{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And He called</b> — the letter alef [in] לילה [night] is added, for it is ma'leh [plene]. And [the word] is always masculine." "Evening is close in meaning to darkness, and it is called thus because the forms were intermixed in it. And morning is the opposite of evening, [for then] a person can distinguish [לבקר] among the forms." "And the meaning of \"day one\" concerns the movement of the sphere. And there is a sod for the darshan: six thousand. And since it was stated that the light is called \"day,\" it is not possible that the evening be called \"day.\" Rather, the meaning is: it was evening, and it was also morning of one day. And if the evening and the morning were one day, why [does it say] \"a second day\"?"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "Reading שיוכל as שיוכל (\"so that one can\"), connected to the explanation of בקר as related to בקר/בינה (distinguishing); the syntax is compressed and the run-on structure preserved as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:34.143663821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}